Decision 76 (docs/reorientation/DECISION_LOG.md) records the publication decision.


1. BodyParts3D: adapted, attribution required
---------------------------------------------

BodyParts3D, © The Database Center for Life Science licensed under CC Attribution 4.0 International

Source:  https://dbarchive.biosciencedbc.jp/en/bodyparts3d/
Terms:   https://dbarchive.biosciencedbc.jp/en/bodyparts3d/lic.html (page last updated 2025/02/27; read 2026-11-05)
Licence: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.en

Files used: BodyParts3D 4.0, PART-OF and IS-A trees. No BodyParts3D mesh is in this repository.

Adaptations in this repository. These are numeric values measured from the meshes, not the
meshes themselves; the changes were landmark and centroid measurement, scaling to a 1.80 m
stature, remapping onto the canonical skeleton, and rounding:

- canonical coordinates in src/character_engine/data/anatomy/human_adult_206.json
  (hips, shoulder girdle, spine, thorax, skull: Decisions 67, 68, 71-74), and everything
  generated from that skeleton (builds/exports/skeleton_serialized.json, the Godot body and
  clips in runtime/godot/addons/character_engine/data/, assets/anatomy/proxies/);
- the value tables in scripts/fix_*.py;
- the name mapping and the numeric summaries in docs/audit/A18 to A30 and in the proposals
  in docs/architecture/.

These values are adaptations of one subject and are marked ESTIMATE. The licensor has not
reviewed or endorsed this project. Anyone reusing them must keep the attribution above and
say that the values were changed. No warranty is given by the licensor.

Discrepancy, disclosed: the headers of the 2013 OBJ files state CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan, while
the licensor's current page states CC BY 4.0. This project follows the current page.

Dated audits, proposals and scripts from before Decision 76 may still say "internal use".
Decision 76 and this file take precedence over that wording.


2. ANSUR II: derived statistics
-------------------------------

Gordon, C.C. et al. (2015). 2012 Anthropometric Survey of U.S. Army Personnel. U.S. Army
Natick Soldier RD&E Center, Report NATICK/TR-15/007. The accompanying U.S. Army memorandum
says "cleared for UNLIMITED PUBLIC RELEASE".

Used for ratios and comparisons (Decision 75, A29, A31). The population is U.S. Army
personnel, not the civilian population. The U.S. Army has not endorsed this project.


